<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17190" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτρεμ-έω</span></b> , fut.<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Pomp.</u>
					58
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Syr.</u>
				2
			</span></i>, etc.: aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠτρέμησα</span>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i> (v. infr.), <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Morb.Sacr.</u>
				14
			</span></i>:—<i>not to tremble, to keep still</i> or
				<i>quiet,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵνα τοι τρίχες ἀτρεμέωσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					539
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδαμά κω ἠτρεμήσαμεν,</span>
			of a restless people, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.8
			</span></i>.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span> (as v.l., cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτρεμίζω</span>), etc.; of a state of health,
				<i>remain stationary,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				1.3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτρεμέει ἡ χολή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>SD</u>
					1.15
				</span></i>
			; of the patient, <i>endure,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχεδὸν οὐκ ἀναπνέων ἠτρέμει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Am.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			, al.; of water, <i>to be calm,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Antyll.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				10.3.9
			</span></i>:—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτρέμ᾽
			ἔσεσθαι</span> shd. be read for inf.
			
				Med.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτρεμέεσθαι</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				47
			</span></i>.—Found in <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Xen.</u>
				977b17
			</span></i>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠρεμέω</span> is the 
				Att.
			 equivalent.</div>
